{"availability":"available","full":"MDRYLA/q2-second-brain-demo","name":"q2-second-brain-demo","description":"Public portfolio version of Q2 — personal Second Brain + Coach app (Next.js 16 + Supabase + E2E AES-GCM client-side encryption). Submitted to Bison Fellowship 2026.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-09T23:23:15Z","updated":"2026-08-03T04:18:04Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://q2-second-brain-demo.vercel.app","topics":["bison-fellowship","e2e-encryption","nextjs","portfolio","react","supabase","tailwindcss","typescript"],"demo":"https://q2-second-brain-demo.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.072Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.072Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.072Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.072Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A personal journaling, planning and habit-tracker app with end-to-end client-side encryption. Two design variants, one codebase. Submitted to Bison Fellowship 2026 as a portfolio artifact.","Q2 is a personal \"Second Brain + Coach\" application. It connects four things that people normally try to track in five different apps:","The app is built around end-to-end client-side encryption: a BIP-39 mnemonic derives an AES-GCM key in the browser; the backend only ever sees ENC: ciphertext. Even the database operator cannot read your journal entries."],"features":["Cascade planning — Year → Quarter → Month → Week → Day, with each level linking to the next.","Daily check-in / check-out — short morning intention, longer evening review, intentionally anti-gamification (no streaks, no XP, no scores).","Knowledge + ideas — markdown notes with inline #tags, freeform journal, quick capture.","An AI coach (server-side, optional) — Claude API runs weekly/monthly/quarterly reviews and confronts the user against their own wri